Making **extra mortgage repayments** is one of the most effective wealth-building strategies available to Australian homeowners. On a $600,000 loan at 6.3% over 30 years, an extra $500 per month reduces the loan term by approximately 8 years and saves over $160,000 in interest. Even modest additional payments early in the loan have a compounding effect because every extra dollar of principal reduces the interest charged in every subsequent month.

This calculator simulates your loan balance month by month with the extra repayment added to your standard repayment. It shows the exact number of years and months saved, total interest saved, and the new payoff date. If you have an offset account, every dollar held there effectively acts as an extra repayment — use this calculator to understand the impact. The year-by-year breakdown table shows your remaining balance at the end of each year under the accelerated repayment schedule.
